# which raises on the same empty slice for the same reason. Both are the same
# mistake made twice, and the traceback still lands after every useful line has
# printed, which is what made it look like noise for twenty rounds.
#
# Guarded now, and CHECKED ON THE HOST before flashing rather than on the board:
# the function is extracted and called on a 1x1 and a 5x5 surface, giving
# "interior EMPTY" and "interior max 0 off>1 0". That is a thing this project
# can test without a flash and had not been.
#
# THE DECISION RULE, WRITTEN BEFORE THE RUN.
#
#   MobileNet prints every line and no traceback
#             the regression set is fully readable and the remaining question
#             is one channel of 1001 at maxdiff 4.
#   it crashes a third time
#             stop patching call sites and find every reduction over a sliced
#             surface at once.
#   any of the four controls moves
#             nothing but perch.py changed, so that could only be this file.
