# Mesa, the kernel and charsiu are byte identical to round 205.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-16 round 205. pw33x64w56 is CORRECT. What is left on MobileNet is one
# channel and a measuring tool that cannot see a one pixel output.
#
# ROUND 204 CLOSED IT, and the before and after are in one log:
#
#   with the term      64 of 64 channels match, every channel correct
#   ROCKET_NO_ICPAD_SUM 18 of 64, COMPUTED 0, b median -31.40
#
# All three controls stayed at every channel correct, as they must: their ic is
# already a multiple of 16 and the padded term is identically zero there.
#
# THE WHOLE CHAIN, three separate places that all counted the real ic:
#
#   r197  the weight buffer, ALIGN(ic,16)          slope 0.44 -> 0.98
#   r202  five CNA registers, from one `ic =`      offset std 69.11 -> 0.85
#   r204  calculate_weight_sum's padded term       correct
#
# and the framing this project carried since round 176, "a pointwise fails on
# input channels above 32", was wrong the whole time: pw64x41w56 has 64 and is
# right. It is ic not being a multiple of SIXTEEN.
